@ez

Am IAMB is a metrical foot in poetry that is an unstressed syllable followed by a stressed syllable. Like da-DA, as opposed to DA-da. Shakespeare’s plays were famously written in iambic pentameter, which is lines of five iambs each. 

And the B is silent. So “I am” being an iamb is apt.

