Babies need to nurse. Moms who are breastfeeding  sometimes have to use pumps. A lactation room allows them to do so in private.

How can that possibly be seen as nauseating or offensive?

@Nancy
I don't think anyone took it that much to heart...  but for some of us, well, a baby who is intubated can't nurse, but once milk production is underway, it's "game ON."  Friends found a La Leche League chapter and borrowed a PUMP for me; I was able to save and freeze breast milk.  One can also express milk by hand...    
I guess it can sound unappealing or unsightly, but not to one on the front lines...  (That baby is now 45.)

